Snackbar
React Query - storing state

understand useEffect
- It keeps an eye on the provided state variable/hook variable
- If any variables in the list changes, it will run the code inside
- ! Can only 'watch' state and hooks, consts wont work

understand useQueryClient
- It takes the closest instance of something at the time it is called
- It hooks that instance into a constant so we can use it
- This includes the content related to that instance (user.id)

react query:
- calls the API if theres nothing there
- deleted the original state, replace it with the new state

